{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-3}{{x}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x-3}{x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-3}{-1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7acf7423-e8b7-5b28-a3d4-100be04f8153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572697 #edb/ref 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & =\\frac{{3}^{3}-9(3)}{{3}^{2}-5(3)+6}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & =\\frac{y({y}^{2}-9)}{(y-2)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y(y-3)(y+3)}{(y-2)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y(y+3)}{(y-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & ={lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{y(y+3)}{y-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3+3)}{3-2} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8c786dd-8e95-5f38-8555-c19baa5a85a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572728 #edb/ref 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & =\\frac{9(0)^{3}-4(0)}{3(0)^{2}+2(0)}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & =\\frac{x(9{x}^{2}-4)}{x(3x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{x}^{2}-4}{3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{2}-4}{3x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-4}{0+2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572732 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572732 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0796118c-90f3-59dc-9c5f-bed198c5fe51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572732 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572769 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572769 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "68972858-a460-50bc-a8a4-057bf06d32dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572769 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572788 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2aabd23-f3ac-5637-91ae-b0a3e28457d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572788 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572697 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
